Phase 4 (Next)

Now we move from "Backend + DB" to a complete ecommerce platform.

Step 1 — Create Orders Table

Inside PostgreSQL:

CREATE TABLE orders (
    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    product_id INT,
    quantity INT,
    order_date TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

Insert sample order:

INSERT INTO orders (product_id, quantity)
VALUES (1,2);

Verify:

SELECT * FROM orders;
Step 2 — Add Order APIs

Current:

GET /products

Add:

GET /orders
POST /orders

Example:

app.post("/orders", async (req, res) => {
  const { product_id, quantity } = req.body;

  const result = await pool.query(
    "INSERT INTO orders(product_id, quantity) VALUES($1,$2) RETURNING *",
    [product_id, quantity]
  );

  res.json(result.rows[0]);
});
Step 3 — DynamoDB

Remember our architecture:

Products & Orders  -> PostgreSQL
Cart              -> DynamoDB
Images            -> S3

Next we'll create DynamoDB using Terraform:

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "cart" {
  name         = "shopping-cart"
  billing_mode = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"

  hash_key = "userId"

  attribute {
    name = "userId"
    type = "S"
  }
}

Then:

POST /cart
GET /cart

will use DynamoDB.

